{
 "id": "FbAdTranscripts01",
 "name": "Transcribe competitor Facebook ads from the Ad Library to Google Sheets with Apify",
 "active": false,
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "sticky-main",
   "name": "Overview",
   "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
   "typeVersion": 1,
   "position": [
    -980,
    -300
   ],
   "parameters": {
    "width": 700,
    "height": 1080,
    "content": "# Transcribe competitor Facebook ads from the Ad Library to Google Sheets with Apify\n\nTurn any Facebook Ad Library search into a spreadsheet of what competitors actually say in their video ads: the first-3-seconds hook, the CTA, the advertiser and the full transcript, one row per ad.\n\n### Who it's for\nMedia buyers, creative strategists and agencies who study competitor video ads at volume and want the spoken words, not just thumbnails.\n\n### How it works\n1. A Set node holds your Ad Library search URL and the number of ads to fetch.\n2. An HTTP Request runs the Facebook Ads Library scraper on Apify and returns the matching video ads.\n3. A second HTTP Request sends those rows to the Facebook Ads Transcript Scraper on Apify, which downloads each video, transcribes the speech and extracts the hook and CTA. Expired links and music-only ads come back as uncharged misses.\n4. A Set node tidies the fields and a Google Sheets node appends one row per ad.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create an HTTP Header Auth credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`) and select it on both HTTP Request nodes.\n2. Connect Google Sheets and pick the spreadsheet and sheet.\n3. Open the Config node, paste any Ad Library search URL (set media_type=video) and choose how many ads to process.\n4. Run the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\nAn Apify account (the free plan's credit covers a 20-ad test run) and a Google account.\n\n### Customization tips\nSwap the scraper for any Ad Library scraper you already use, the transcript step reads its rows by video URL. Replace the Google Sheets node with Airtable, Slack or a database. Add a Schedule Trigger to run it weekly.\n"
   }
  },
  {
